<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cillium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cillium was a Roman town in the province of Byzacena, at the site of modern Kasserine in west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, still known for its triumphal arch and mausoleums. In 544 the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> was defeated and killed near it by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antalas">Antalas</a> and his allies, a blow to Byzantine rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div>
